---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import ParticipationNativeHistory from './ParticipationNativeHistory.astro';
type Row = { year: string; weight_field: string; scope: string; dimension: string; group: string;
	n: string; modeled_voter_pct: string; modeled_nonvoter_pct: string;
	already_voted_self_report_pct: string };
const { names } = Astro.props as { names: Record<string, string> };
const base = 'data/participation-ap-history/20261108-01/';
const result: { national_overall: Row[] } = JSON.parse(readFileSync(base + 'summary.json', 'utf8'));
const download = JSON.parse(readFileSync(base + 'download.json', 'utf8'));
const states = Object.keys(names).filter(code => !['US', 'DC'].includes(code)).sort();
const pct = (value: string) => `${Number(value).toFixed(2)}%`;
---

<section id="participation-ap-history" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="ap-history-title"
	data-ap-source={download.viewer.url} data-ap-sha256={download.viewer.sha256}
	data-publication-class="source-weighted-repeated-cross-section-descriptive">
	<h3 id="ap-history-title">Historical voter-and-nonvoter studies: 2018 to 2024</h3>
	<p>AP/NORC VoteCast provides separate source-weighted participation descriptions for
		<strong>2018, 2020, 2022 and 2024</strong>. These are modeled participation shares in each
		study's registered-source frame, <strong>not administratively observed turnout or a linked panel</strong>.
		Native poll-close and final weights are separate views of the same respondents, not independent samples.</p>
	<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Historical national source-frame participation">
		<table><caption>All eight national source/weight views. Same-year rows reuse respondents; do not sum them.</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">Year</th><th scope="col">Native weights</th><th scope="col">Modeled voter</th>
				<th scope="col">Modeled nonvoter</th><th scope="col">Self-reported already voted</th>
				<th scope="col">Source n</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>{result.national_overall.map(row => <tr data-ap-overall={`${row.year}:${row.weight_field}`}>
				<th scope="row">{row.year}</th>
				<td>{row.weight_field.startsWith('FINALVOTE') ? 'Final' : 'Poll-close'}</td>
				<td data-ap-voter>{pct(row.modeled_voter_pct)}</td>
				<td data-ap-nonvoter>{pct(row.modeled_nonvoter_pct)}</td>
				<td data-ap-reported>{pct(row.already_voted_self_report_pct)}</td>
				<td>{Number(row.n).toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
			</tr>)}</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p data-ap-status role="status">The national table and complete downloads work without JavaScript.
		Open research to load the selected state and national-group views.</p>
	<fieldset data-ap-controls disabled>
		<legend>Explore the permitted historical source aggregates</legend>
		<label>Election year
			<select data-ap-year><option>2018</option><option>2020</option><option>2022</option><option selected>2024</option></select>
		</label>
		<label>Native weights
			<select data-ap-frame><option value="FINALVOTE">Final</option><option value="POLLCLOSE">Poll-close</option></select>
		</label>
		<label>Source scope
			<select data-ap-scope><option value="US50_SOURCE">National source: 50 states, no D.C.</option>
				{states.map(code => <option value={code}>{names[code]}</option>)}
			</select>
		</label>
	</fieldset>
	<div data-ap-dynamic hidden>
		<p data-ap-qualification></p>
		<p><code data-ap-weight></code></p>
		<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Selected historical participation view">
			<table><caption data-ap-caption></caption>
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">Source group</th><th scope="col">Modeled voter</th>
					<th scope="col">Modeled nonvoter</th><th scope="col">Self-reported already voted</th>
					<th scope="col">Source n</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody data-ap-rows></tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</div>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Source frames, changing groups and withheld estimates</summary>
		<p>2018 state values are source descriptives only: the publisher reports estimates for
			<strong>47 inference states despite sampling all 50</strong>. Delaware and West Virginia
			<strong>2022 state inference is withheld</strong>. A documented 2022 race field,
			<code>RACETH5</code>, was absent from the released file and is not reconstructed.</p>
		<p>Native SEX/GENDER and race/ethnicity definitions differ across years. Current group membership
			is not a fixed historical cohort. State demographics remain private; no state survey estimate
			is allocated to counties or precincts. Unknown and disclosure-removed responses remain in the
			full overall denominators, not recovered or redistributed.</p>
		<p>The broad selection requires 500 positive-weight source cases for whole-state overall rows
			and 1,000 for national groups. This is <strong>not an anonymity or precision guarantee</strong>;
			raw per-model-class support is not available in the cached statistics. Weight units are not
			population people, and no confidence interval is invented.</p>
		<p>Final weights reflect outcome calibration, not independent outcome validation.
			These repeated cross-sections are not a linked panel. No cross-study turnout change or
			individual switching estimate is inferred by joining AP rows to Civic.</p>
	</details>
	<p>The complete selected package contains <strong>602 participation rows and all 710 broad-query
		selection decisions</strong>, including withheld requests. It includes all permitted aggregate
		inputs, full queries, source hashes, code and tests, not respondent records or private fine cells.</p>
	<p>{download.assets.map((asset: { name: string; url: string }, index: number) => <>
		{index > 0 && ' | '}<a href={asset.url} data-ap-download={asset.name}>
			{asset.name === 'complete-analysis.zip' ? 'Complete historical AP analysis (ZIP)' : asset.name}
		</a>
	</>)}</p>
	<ParticipationNativeHistory names={names} />
</section>
<script is:inline type="module" src="/scripts/participation-ap-history.js"></script>
<style>
	#participation-ap-history { min-width: 0; }
	fieldset { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .75rem 1rem; margin-block: 1rem; }
	label { display: grid; gap: .25rem; min-width: 0; max-width: 100%; }
	select { min-height: 2.5rem; max-width: 100%; }
	code { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
